--- import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro"; import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro"; import "../../styles/standards-poster.css"; import "../../styles/extended.css"; import metadata from "../../data/standards/japangaap/asbj18.json"; --- <StandardPageLayout code={metadata.code} standardType={metadata.framework} title={metadata.title} description={metadata.description} issued={metadata.issued} latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment} status={metadata.status} summary={metadata.summary} bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice} > <Fragment slot="toc"> <PageToc items={[{"id":"s1","label":"Conceptual Framework Linkage"},{"id":"s2","label":"Scope"},{"id":"s3","label":"Recognition Criteria — a Legal Obligation Tied to Asset Retirement"},{"id":"s4","label":"Initial Measurement — Present Value of Estimated Future Cash Outflows"},{"id":"s5","label":"The Corresponding Asset — Added to the Related Asset's Cost"},{"id":"s6","label":"Accretion of the Liability Over Time"},{"id":"s7","label":"Subsequent Remeasurement"},{"id":"s8","label":"Worked Example — Initial Recognition of an Asset Retirement Obligation"},{"id":"s9","label":"Worked Example — Accretion Expense Over Time"},{"id":"s10","label":"Disclosure Requirements"},{"id":"s11","label":"Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates"},{"id":"s12","label":"Relationship to IAS/IFRS and US GAAP"},{"id":"s13","label":"Statement Mapping"},{"id":"s14","label":"Related Standards"},{"id":"s15","label":"Glossary"}]} /> </Fragment> <div class="wrap"> <div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Recognising the genuine future cost of dismantling or restoring an asset</div><div class="principle">ASBJ Statement No. 18 requires recognition of a LIABILITY for LEGAL obligations to DISMANTLE, REMOVE, or RESTORE a tangible fixed asset at the END of its useful life — such as decommissioning a facility, or RESTORING leased premises to their ORIGINAL condition upon lease expiry. Rather than recognising this cost only when the retirement ACTUALLY occurs (potentially decades later), the OBLIGATION is recognised as soon as it ARISES, measured at PRESENT VALUE.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Legal obligations tied to the retirement of tangible fixed assets</div><div class="principle">This Statement applies to LEGAL obligations (arising from law, contract, or similar binding requirement) associated with the RETIREMENT of tangible fixed assets — including owned facilities subject to decommissioning laws and LEASED premises subject to restoration/original-condition clauses.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Recognition Criteria — a Legal Obligation Tied to Asset Retirement</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Must be a genuine legal obligation, not merely an expected future cost</div><div class="text-supporting">A liability is recognised ONLY where a genuine LEGAL obligation exists — arising from a LAW, REGULATION, or CONTRACTUAL requirement (e.g. a lease agreement requiring restoration of the premises to their original condition) — tied DIRECTLY to the eventual RETIREMENT of a specific tangible fixed asset. A merely EXPECTED future cost, WITHOUT an underlying legal obligation, does NOT qualify for recognition under this Statement.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Initial Measurement — Present Value of Estimated Future Cash Outflows</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Discounted using a risk-free rate reflecting the time value of money</div><div class="text-supporting">The asset retirement obligation is initially measured at the PRESENT VALUE of the ESTIMATED future cash outflows required to satisfy the obligation, DISCOUNTED using a rate reflecting the TIME VALUE of money (generally a RISK-FREE rate appropriate to the estimated timing of the future cash outflow) — recognising that a future obligation is WORTH LESS today than its eventual settlement amount.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>The Corresponding Asset — Added to the Related Asset's Cost</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Capitalised and depreciated alongside the underlying asset</div><div class="text-supporting">The SAME amount initially recognised as a LIABILITY is ALSO added to the CARRYING AMOUNT of the RELATED tangible fixed asset — reflecting that the future retirement cost is a genuine, unavoidable PART of the total cost of ACQUIRING and USING that asset. This capitalised amount is then DEPRECIATED over the asset's remaining USEFUL LIFE, alongside the asset's other costs.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Accretion of the Liability Over Time</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">The discount unwinds as an expense each period</div><div class="text-supporting">As TIME passes and the eventual SETTLEMENT date draws closer, the DISCOUNTED liability is INCREASED each period to reflect the UNWINDING of the discount — recognised as an "ACCRETION EXPENSE" (or interest expense) in the Statement of Income, GRADUALLY building the liability up TOWARD its eventual, undiscounted settlement amount.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Subsequent Remeasurement</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Revised for changes in estimated cash outflows or timing</div><div class="text-supporting">Where the ESTIMATED amount or TIMING of future cash outflows CHANGES (e.g. due to revised cost estimates or regulatory changes), the liability is REMEASURED, with the CORRESPONDING adjustment generally made to the RELATED asset's carrying amount (rather than immediately through profit or loss), consistent with the ORIGINAL capitalisation approach.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Initial Recognition of an Asset Retirement Obligation</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Recognising the present value of a future restoration cost</div> <div class="worked"><div class="wk-title">Example: A leased retail store requiring restoration</div><div class="wk-body">A company leases retail space, with a LEGAL obligation under the lease to RESTORE the premises to their original condition at the end of the 10-year lease term. The estimated future restoration cost is ¥30,000,000, and the present value using an appropriate discount rate is ¥22,000,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company recognises a <strong>¥22,000,000 ASSET RETIREMENT OBLIGATION</strong> (liability), with a MATCHING ¥22,000,000 added to the CARRYING AMOUNT of the related leasehold improvement asset — to be DEPRECIATED over the 10-year lease term alongside the asset's other costs.</div></div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Accretion Expense Over Time</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Unwinding the discount each period</div> <div class="worked"><div class="wk-title">Example: Year 1 accretion on the ¥22,000,000 obligation</div><div class="wk-body">Continuing the prior example, the discount rate used was 4%.</div><div class="wk-answer">Year 1 ACCRETION EXPENSE = ¥22,000,000 × 4% = <strong>¥880,000</strong> — recognised as an EXPENSE in the Statement of Income, INCREASING the liability to ¥22,880,000 at the end of Year 1 — this UNWINDING process CONTINUES each year, GRADUALLY building the liability toward its full ¥30,000,000 undiscounted amount by the END of the 10-year lease term.</div></div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBJ Statement No. 18 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Nature of asset retirement obligations and how the liability amount is calculated</span><span>Movement in the liability during the period (recognition, accretion, settlement, remeasurement)</span><span>Discount rate and other key assumptions used</span></div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div> <div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether a genuine legal obligation exists, as opposed to a merely anticipated future cost</span></div></div> <div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Estimated future cash outflows required to satisfy the obligation</span><span>Discount rate and expected timing of settlement</span></div></div></div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS/IFRS and US GAAP</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — J-GAAP vs IFRS and US GAAP</div><div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-1-1-1"><span>Feature</span><span>J-GAAP (ASBJ Statement No. 18)</span><span>IFRS (IAS 37/IFRIC 1) / US GAAP (ASC 410)</span></div> <div class="tr cols-1-1-1"><span>Present value initial measurement</span><span>YES</span><span>YES — converged with both frameworks</span></div> <div class="tr cols-1-1-1"><span>Corresponding asset capitalisation</span><span>YES</span><span>YES — converged with both frameworks</span></div> <div class="tr cols-1-1-1"><span>Accretion of the liability over time</span><span>YES, as an expense</span><span>YES, as an expense — converged with both frameworks</span></div> </div> <div class="note">This is one of the MOST genuinely converged standards in the ENTIRE J-GAAP suite — its development drew directly on BOTH the international IAS 37/IFRIC 1 framework and the equivalent US GAAP standard (SFAS 143, now ASC 410), reflecting a period of Japan's convergence project drawing on MULTIPLE international sources simultaneously.</div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every asset retirement obligation event lands</div><div class="th cols-16-1-14"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div> <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Initial recognition</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Liability and corresponding asset both recognised</span></div> <div class="tr cols-16-1-14"><span>Accretion expense</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span></span><span>Recognised each period as the discount unwinds</span> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div><div class="td-table"><div class="th cols-08-2"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div> <div class="tr cols-08-2"><span>ASBJ Statement No. 34</span><span>Leases — asset retirement obligations frequently arise in connection with leasehold restoration clauses</span></div> </div> </div> </div><div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div><div class="grid"> <div class="card cn span2"> <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Asset retirement obligation (資産除去債務)</div><div class="glossary-def">A legal obligation to dismantle, remove, or restore a tangible fixed asset at the end of its useful life, recognised at present value.</div></div> <div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Accretion expense</div><div class="glossary-def">The periodic expense recognised as the discount on an asset retirement obligation unwinds over time.</div></div> </div> </div><div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Japan GAAP terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><span class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (貸借対照表)</span><span class="litem"><span class="badge bp">P&amp;L</span> Statement of Income / Profit and Loss Statement (損益計算書)</span><span class="litem"><span class="badge bo">Net Assets</span> 純資産の部</span><span class="litem"><span class="badge be">SCNA</span> Statement of Changes in Net Assets (株主資本等変動計算書)</span><span class="litem"><span class="badge bc">SCF</span> Statement of Cash Flows (キャッシュ・フロー計算書)</span></div></div> </div> </StandardPageLayout> 